@startuml
title Zhiyan Tongjie Requirements Review Checklist & Report - System Architecture

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

' Context actors
rectangle "Reviewer" as Reviewer
rectangle "Requirements Owner" as Owner
rectangle "Developer" as Dev
rectangle "Tester" as Tester
rectangle "Project Stakeholder" as Stakeholder

artifact "Requirements Document\nUnder Review" as ReqDoc
folder "Standards & Specifications\n- Industry standards\n- Product specs\n- Business rules\n- Documentation norms" as Standards

node "Markdown-capable Environment\n(Editor/Viewer)" as MDEnv

' Artifact components
artifact "Checklist Template (Markdown)" <<Template>> as Template
artifact "Review Report (Markdown)" <<Review Artifact>> as Report

' Structure of Review Report
package "Review Artifact Structure" {
  component "Objectives & Basis" as Sec1
  component "Completeness" as SecComp
  component "Exceptions & Auxiliary" as SecEx
  component "Understandability" as SecUnd
  component "Model Accuracy" as SecModel
  component "Extension & Improvement" as SecExt
  component "Problem Report" as SecProb
  component "Scoring (4 x 10 + Total 40)" as SecScore
  component "Reviewer Metadata" as SecMeta
}

' Containment (visual)
Report -down- Sec1
Report -down- SecComp
Report -down- SecEx
Report -down- SecUnd
Report -down- SecModel
Report -down- SecExt
Report -down- SecProb
Report -down- SecScore
Report -down- SecMeta

' Data requirements mapped
note right of Sec1
DR-001: Review purpose (goal, method, report purpose, basis)
FR-001: Define objectives and methods
FR-002: Standards-based review
C-001, C-002 apply
end note

note right of SecComp
FR-003: Core/basic functions align with user needs
NFR-001: Completeness checks
end note

note right of SecEx
FR-004: Special cases, exceptions, auxiliary functions
NFR-001 applies
end note

note right of SecUnd
FR-005: Clarity, understandability, specificity, detail, refinement
NFR-002: Understandability checks
end note

note right of SecModel
FR-006: Conformance, reasonableness, rigor, accuracy of models
NFR-003: Model quality checks
end note

note right of SecExt
FR-007: Extension & improvement goals are clear, feasible, concrete, demonstrable
end note

note right of SecProb
FR-008 / DR-003: Problems, overall evaluation, improvement suggestions
end note

note right of SecScore
FR-009 / DR-004: Four 10-point dimensions + total (out of 40)
NFR-004, C-003 apply
end note

note right of SecMeta
FR-010 / DR-005: Reviewer identity and review date
end note

' Flows and interactions
Reviewer -[#blue]-> MDEnv : edits/inspects
MDEnv -[#green]-> Template : uses checklist
Reviewer -[#blue]-> Template : initiates review (FR-001)
Template -[#brown]-> Report : instantiated as review report
Reviewer -[#blue]-> Report : fills sections, records findings
Report -[#gray]-> ReqDoc : inspects requirement content (FR-003..FR-007)
Report -[#gray]-> Standards : references basis (FR-002, C-002)
MDEnv -[#green]-> Report : stores/displays Markdown

' Score aggregation
SecComp -[dashed,#darkgray]-> SecScore : dimension score
SecUnd -[dashed,#darkgray]-> SecScore : dimension score
SecModel -[dashed,#darkgray]-> SecScore : dimension score
SecExt -[dashed,#darkgray]-> SecScore : dimension score

' Consumers of the review report
Owner -[#purple]-> Report : receives findings & suggestions
Dev -[#purple]-> Report : consumes review findings
Tester -[#purple]-> Report : consumes review findings
Stakeholder -[#purple]-> Report : reads concise result

' Constraints / assumptions
note bottom of Template
C-004: Business-specific functional requirements are outside this checklist.
end note

note bottom of Report
Format: Markdown checklist incl. items, scores, reviewer metadata, comments.
Data exchange: single Markdown file artifact
end note

@enduml
